    "narrative": "Today, we\u2019re leaning into **Brayan Rocchio** as our strongest play at 43.07. While his base projection was 48.60, a confluence of factors has him firmly in the starting lineup. The slight decrease in score from his base projection is attributed to a -6% park adjustment, a -2% dynamic platoon advantage against a right-handed pitcher, and him hitting 9th in the order (-8%). However, a +7% boost from facing Peralta, F (R) with a 4.32 SP_xERA, coupled with a 100% recency boost, solidifies his starting role despite the lower order spot.\n\nOur bench features a few players we're keeping a close eye on. **Liam Hicks** was the most compelling option just missing the cut, scoring 31.07. His base projection was 44.39, but a combination of a -6% park factor, a significant -12% SP skill adjustment against a left-handed pitcher, an -11% dynamic platoon disadvantage, and an -6% hit for batting 8th in the lineup, ultimately pushed him below our established floor of 40.0. It\u2019s a tough squeeze for playing time, especially when factoring in the presence of players like **Gunnar Henderson**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jackson Merrill** who have higher projections and are penciled in. Notably, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Kyle Tucker** have team off-days, while **Luis Robert Jr.** remains on the Injured List, as flagged by the \ud83d\udea8 INJURED (IL) warning.",
